## CLAIM ef6b75ef/131 — who can dispatch the animator vtable slots (static)

Provenance **arena/ef6b75ef**, branch `arena/ef6b75ef-windwings-space-shooter-game-p` (HEAD `3e259c6aa`), #27 static native lane. Follows official 130 handoff **6427817329**, whose review question 1 was: is "virtual-only, zero direct refs" enough, or must the next cycle scan indirect slot loads?

**Bounded scope (one layer):** a pure static scan of the pinned `libunity.so` for
1. every `ADRP+ADD` reference to the animator vtable family (`10b0c80`, `10b0f98`, `10b1100`, `10b1130`, `10b0f30`, `10b1240`, `10b1420`, `10b1150`, `10b1330`);
2. every `LDR Xt,[Xb,#off]` load of the four recovered slot offsets {2→0x10, 3→0x18, 31→0xf8, 33→0x108} that is followed within 8 instructions by `BLR Xt`, with base-register provenance (`vptr_from_x0` / `adrp_base` / `unknown`) and the owning FDE;
3. `ADRP+ADD` references to the six containers already used by 130 (`0x10ecb08`, `0x10e18b0`, `0x10e19c8/0x10e19d0`, `0x10e18f8/0x10e18b8`);
4. one caller level (BL/B) for the owners of those sites.

**No** instruction is executed, **no** serialized/runtime value is invented, **no** class name is asserted, **no** self-ACK, **no** #27-full closure, **no** PR merge/main push, **no** other lane takeover. Deliverables: `reverse-engineering/raw/owner131/probe.json.gz`, `datas/l3_ef6b75ef131_native_vtable_dispatch.json.gz`, `tools/recovery/owner131.py`, `tools/verify/owner131.py`, `tests/test_owner131.py`, report `docs/apk-analysis/131-ef6b75ef-native-vtable-dispatch.md`, verification receipts. Static-only per 6418032974 / 6418326986.
